---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from './Eyebrow.astro';
import StatCard from './StatCard.astro';
import VerificationChart from './VerificationChart.astro';

const bars = [
  {
    label: 'Classic repair tool (GenProg)',
    value: 2,
    display: '2%',
    note: '98% were overfitting',
  },
  {
    label: 'Strong 2024 frontier method (D4C)',
    value: 50,
    display: '~50%',
    note: 'roughly a coin flip',
  },
  {
    label: 'Five frontier models on 20 real CVEs, 2026',
    value: 50,
    display: '50%',
    note: 'best solve rate',
  },
];

const stats = [
  {
    value: '45%',
    label:
      'of AI-generated code introduces an OWASP-class vulnerability, and the rate is flat across model generations.',
    source: 'Veracode, 100+ LLMs, 2025',
  },
  {
    value: '42%',
    label: 'of committed code is now AI-generated.',
    source: 'Sonar, 1,100+ developers, 2026',
  },
  {
    value: '24%',
    label: 'of developers merge AI code without reviewing it at all.',
    source: 'Qodo, 2025',
  },
  {
    value: '43%',
    label: 'of AI code changes need debugging in production.',
    source: 'Lightrun, 2026',
  },
];
---

<Section id="verification-gap">
  <Eyebrow class="reveal">The verification gap</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
    A patch can pass every test and leave the hole wide open.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.06fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="space-y-7">
      <p class="reveal text-[17px] leading-[1.6]">
        Software is checked by tests. A test is a handful of examples of what the code
        should do. It is{' '}
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">a sample, not a specification</strong>.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-2" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
        When you tell an AI to make the tests pass, it{' '}
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">optimises for the sample</strong>. Passing the
        tests tells you the sample is satisfied and very little else.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-2" style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
        Researchers have studied this for over a decade and named it{' '}
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">overfitting</strong>.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-2" style="--reveal-delay:180ms">
        The industry checks AI fixes by re-running the scanner. The AI was optimising to
        make that scanner go quiet.{' '}
        <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">It is a circular test.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <VerificationChart
      title="Test-passing patches that were actually correct"
      caption="Sources: Qi et al. via Invalidator (arXiv 2301.01113) · D4C 2024 · independent CVE study, May 2026"
      bars={bars}
      class="lg:pt-1"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mt-20 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:mt-24 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      stats.map((stat, i) => (
        <div class="reveal flex" style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 60}ms`}>
          <StatCard
            value={stat.value}
            label={stat.label}
            source={stat.source}
            class="flex-1"
          />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <blockquote
    class="reveal mt-20 border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 lg:mt-24 lg:pl-8"
  >
    <p class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.018em] lg:text-[27px]" style="max-width:28ch">
      &ldquo;The alert turning green and the bug being fixed are two different events.
      The industry measures the first one.&rdquo;
    </p>
  </blockquote>
</Section>
